### Summary of the Decision
**Redis Streams** was chosen over Apache Kafka. Given the team constraint of only 6 engineers with no dedicated infrastructure specialist, a 2-week time-to-value delivery target, zero team experience with Kafka, and a modest budget, Redis Streams represents the optimal choice. 

A single Redis instance can easily scale past the 10x peak load requirement (5,000 req/s), while utilizing existing production Redis infrastructure eliminates any setup delays or operational overhead. Exactly-once semantics for billing-critical events are achieved by pairing an **at-least-once transport guarantee** (via Redis Streams consumer groups, PEL tracking, and message acknowledgements) with **idempotent consumption** at the application and database layer using PostgreSQL transactions and unique event ID constraints. This delivers the robust reliability of exactly-once processing without any of the immense operational complexity or infrastructure cost of Kafka.
